[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2588176840","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101497#issuecomment-2588176840","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101497","id":2588176840,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aRHHI","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-13T20:53:47Z","updated_at":"2025-01-13T20:53:47Z","body":"For further detail, we handle Glow in a very weird way. We tonemap the input color, then we tonemap the glow result, then we add them together in sRGB space\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/d19147e09a13a7d6df44076f15893a5d1108fbb0/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/effects/tonemap.glsl#L575-L580\n\nThis means that additive glow ends up with all the negative effects of adding light in sRGB space. Using any of the other glow modes would look better. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2588176840/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2603054213","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101497#issuecomment-2603054213","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101497","id":2603054213,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bJ3SF","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-20T18:38:42Z","updated_at":"2025-01-20T18:38:42Z","body":"I recall there was a reason why we perform glow after tonemapping, but I don't remember why exactly. It might have to do with MSAA/FXAA quality.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2603054213/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2852256146","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101497#issuecomment-2852256146","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101497","id":2852256146,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6qAfmS","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-05T20:28:48Z","updated_at":"2025-05-05T20:31:35Z","body":"I've attempted this: https://github.com/Calinou/godot/tree/glow-perform-before-tonemapping\n\nWhen using AgX, it looks nice with the Additive glow mode, but using Screen or Softlight means glowing pixels will never be able to be fully white:\n\nAdditive | Screen | Softlight\n-|-|-\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7da956ee-46ef-49ab-95b1-4600f63802c2) | ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cbc60efd-06ad-4440-9977-c9707a808963) | ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/42910224-4e3f-44fd-b611-981c7e30ab11)\n\nFor reference, Replace looks like this:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1ad82d73-4a24-410b-8359-c145bef2a99a)\n\nAdditionally, the Screen mode will sometimes look strange, creating an unexpected shift towards green in this scene:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8ffc102f-7b08-4d2d-b7e5-3bd962d36083\n\nHere are videos before/after the change (first one is `master`, second one is with this change):\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/51eb445a-e185-4d8e-9687-793a4fcfdebb\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/72ff24e3-bd47-44af-8342-bd46d3daa6be\n\nIn Compatibility, glow already seems to be applied before tonemapping, so my branch affects Forward+ and Mobile only. FXAA and MSAA still seem to work correctly so far, along with TAA and FSR2.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2852256146/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2919794666","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101497#issuecomment-2919794666","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101497","id":2919794666,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uCIfq","user":{"login":"beicause","id":75941842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1OTQxODQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75941842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause","html_url":"https://github.com/beicause","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-29T15:40:12Z","updated_at":"2025-05-29T15:40:12Z","body":"This seems to be the reason why glow is applied in the current way https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/19361#issuecomment-394367510\n\nHonestly, I don't see the benefits of the current weird approach.\n\nJust for reference, Unity documents bloom should be applied before tonemapping: https://docs.unity3d.com/530/Documentation/Manual/script-Tonemapping.html#:~:text=Make%20sure%20that%20Bloom%20should,Depth%20of%20Field%20image%20effect\n\nAnd Bevy also applys bloom before tonemapping: https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/discussions/6655#discussioncomment-4163388","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2919794666/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2921882611","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101497#issuecomment-2921882611","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101497","id":2921882611,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uKGPz","user":{"login":"beicause","id":75941842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1OTQxODQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75941842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause","html_url":"https://github.com/beicause","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-30T10:03:40Z","updated_at":"2025-05-30T11:11:29Z","body":">I've attempted this: https://github.com/Calinou/godot/tree/glow-perform-before-tonemapping\n>When using AgX, it looks nice with the Additive glow mode, but using Screen or Softlight means glowing pixels will never be able to be fully white:\n\n@Calinou Note that Screen or Softlight mode clamps glow to [0, 1]. Could this cause the glow to be too weak when mixed with color?\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/b89c47bb8511433440e5e547afe4459ca3383090/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/effects/tonemap.glsl#L403-L422\n\nEdit: Screen and Softlight doesn't seem to support HDR colors. It might be a reason why glow is applied after tonemapping.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2921882611/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2922305275","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101497#issuecomment-2922305275","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101497","id":2922305275,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uLtb7","user":{"login":"EaryChow","id":59176246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MTc2MjQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59176246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow","html_url":"https://github.com/EaryChow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-30T12:46:18Z","updated_at":"2025-05-30T12:46:48Z","body":"Operations like `screen` and `Softlight` were designed for editing formed image's display pixel strength percentage from 0 to 100% (or 1.0), while glow is more of a lens thing, it is more a light-like behavior that should be a part of the pre-image-formation exposure data, the Additive mode is the only one that actually makes sense anyways.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2922305275/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]